  "limits": [
    "All XR lifecycle tests use an isolated mock runtime and owned synthetic images, not Diablo or SteamVR.",
    "advance(false) never starts a frame; advance(true) can block in xrWaitFrame. Other XR and producer calls have no hard real-time guarantee.",
    "The caller must serialize construction, advances, teardown and borrowed-queue access. There is no concurrent game consumer thread or integration with the game render cycle.",
    "Cleanup can block and fatal runtime/device loss can prevent successful cleanup calls.",
    "The real producer must render both requested eye poses from a coherent scene. Sequential game captures must not be relabeled to pass the strict receipts.",
    "No real game image submitted to an XR runtime, no new headset trial. Prior internal SteamVR validation errors remain unresolved.",
    "Windows D3D12 rendering backend and game resource snapshot/replay closure remain unimplemented."
